  m_Name: VHM_Heart
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  modelName: Male Human Heart
  organType: Heart
  description: "A 3D model of a male human heart from the Human Reference Atlas 2.4.
    Contains approximately 690,000 mapped cells \u2014 roughly twice the female dataset."
  uberonId: UBERON:0002079
  sex: male
  contextualData: "This is the Human Reference Atlas 2.4 male human heart model (UBERON:0000948),
    part of the Human Reference Atlas built by the HuBMAP consortium.\n\nAnatomical
    structures (by mapped cell count):\n- Heart left ventricle: the largest and most
    cell-dense region, responsible for pumping oxygenated blood to the body.\n- Heart
    right ventricle: pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs.\n- Interventricular septum:
    the muscular wall dividing the two ventricles.\n- Left cardiac atrium: receives
    oxygenated blood from the lungs.\n- Right cardiac atrium: receives deoxygenated
    blood from the body.\n- Papillary muscles: anchor the mitral and tricuspid valve
    leaflets, preventing backflow during contraction.\n\nDominant cell types (Azimuth
    annotation):\nVentricular Cardiomyocytes are the most prevalent \u2014 the contractile
    muscle cells responsible for the heartbeat. Fibroblasts are the second most common,
    providing structural support through extracellular matrix production. Other significant
    types include PC1_vent (pericytes lining small vessels), vCM1 (a ventricular
    cardiomyocyte subtype), Capillary Endothelial cells (lining the blood vessels),
    EC1_cap, and Pericytes. The male heart tends to have a higher total cell count
    than the female model due to greater organ mass.\n\nKey biomarkers:\n- Ventricular
    Cardiomyocytes: MYH7, TNNT2, MYL2\n- Fibroblasts: VIM, COL1A1, PDGFRA\n- Capillary
    Endothelial cells: PECAM1 (CD31), CDH5\n- Pericytes: PDGFRB, RGS5\n\nBoth Azimuth
    and CellTypist annotation tools agree that the left ventricle is dominated by
    Ventricular Cardiomyocytes and Fibroblasts. Compared to the female heart model,
    the male heart shows similar cell type proportions but differs in absolute cell
    counts and slight structural volume differences.\n\nData source: HRA v2.4, HuBMAP
    consortium. ASCT+B table peer-reviewed and published in Nature Cell Biology (B\xF6rner
    et al., 2021). Male model identifier: VHM_Heart."
